# Auth Setup Exploration — Notely (Next.js App Router)

## Summary up front
This is a small "Notely" app currently using **NextAuth.js v5 (Auth.js) beta** with two providers (Google OAuth + Credentials/email-password), backed by an **in-memory user store** (no real database). There is also a `docs/clerk.md` + `llms.txt` file already in the repo pointing at Clerk's Next.js quickstart — a strong signal the intended direction is to migrate this app to Clerk (or extend it with magic-link/email sign-in and an `/account` page). Below is everything needed to do that migration/extension.

---

## 1. Core auth files (full contents)

### `src/auth.ts`
```ts
import NextAuth from "next-auth";
import Credentials from "next-auth/providers/credentials";
import Google from "next-auth/providers/google";
import { findOrCreateOAuthUser, verifyPassword } from "@/lib/users";

export const { handlers, signIn, signOut, auth } = NextAuth({
  providers: [
    Google({
      clientId: process.env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID,
      clientSecret: process.env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET,
    }),
    Credentials({
      name: "Email and password",
      credentials: {
        email: { label: "Email", type: "email" },
        password: { label: "Password", type: "password" },
      },
      authorize: async (credentials) => {
        const email = credentials?.email;
        const password = credentials?.password;
        if (typeof email !== "string" || typeof password !== "string") return null;

        const user = await verifyPassword(email, password);
        if (!user) return null;

        return { id: user.id, email: user.email, name: user.name };
      },
    }),
  ],
  session: { strategy: "jwt" },
  pages: {
    signIn: "/signin",
  },
  callbacks: {
    async signIn({ user, account }) {
      // Provision (or link to) a local user record on first Google sign-in.
      if (account?.provider === "google" && user.email) {
        await findOrCreateOAuthUser({
          email: user.email,
          name: user.name ?? user.email,
        });
      }
      return true;
    },
  },
});
```
Exports `handlers`, `signIn`, `signOut`, `auth` — the standard Auth.js v5 pattern.

### `src/lib/users.ts` (in-memory "database")
```ts
import bcrypt from "bcryptjs";

export type User = {
  id: string;
  email: string;
  name: string;
  createdAt: string;
  passwordHash?: string; // absent for OAuth-only users
};

// Pinned on globalThis to survive Turbopack module duplication in dev.
const globalForUsers = globalThis as unknown as { __notelyUsers?: User[] };

const users: User[] =
  globalForUsers.__notelyUsers ??
  (globalForUsers.__notelyUsers = [
    { id: "1", email: "ada@example.com", name: "Ada", createdAt: "2026-01-04" },
    { id: "2", email: "grace@example.com", name: "Grace", createdAt: "2026-02-11" },
  ]);

export async function listUsers(): Promise<User[]> { return users; }
export async function getUser(id: string): Promise<User | undefined> { ... }
export async function getUserByEmail(email: string): Promise<User | undefined> { ... }

export async function createUser({ email, name, password }): Promise<User> {
  // throws if email exists; bcrypt.hash(password, 10)
}

export async function verifyPassword(email, password): Promise<User | undefined> {
  // bcrypt.compare against passwordHash
}

export async function findOrCreateOAuthUser({ email, name }): Promise<User> {
  // used by Google sign-in callback in auth.ts
}

export async function getCurrentUser(): Promise<User | undefined> {
  const { auth } = await import("@/auth"); // lazy import to avoid module cycle
  const session = await auth();
  if (!session?.user?.email) return undefined;
  return getUserByEmail(session.user.email);
}
```
**There is no database** — `users` is a plain array kept alive via `globalThis`. It resets whenever the process restarts. There is no schema/migration/ORM anywhere in the repo.

### Route handler: `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts`
```ts
import { handlers } from "@/auth";
export const { GET, POST } = handlers;
```

### Custom sign-up API: `src/app/api/signup/route.ts`
```ts
import { NextResponse } from "next/server";
import { createUser, getUserByEmail } from "@/lib/users";

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const body = await req.json().catch(() => null);
  const email = typeof body?.email === "string" ? body.email.trim() : "";
  const password = typeof body?.password === "string" ? body.password : "";
  const name = typeof body?.name === "string" && body.name.trim() ? body.name.trim() : email.split("@")[0];

  if (!email || !email.includes("@")) return NextResponse.json({ error: "Enter a valid email address." }, { status: 400 });
  if (password.length < 8) return NextResponse.json({ error: "Password must be at least 8 characters." }, { status: 400 });
  if (await getUserByEmail(email)) return NextResponse.json({ error: "An account with that email already exists." }, { status: 409 });

  await createUser({ email, name, password });
  return NextResponse.json({ ok: true });
