```
- No email-sending library (no nodemailer, resend, etc.) — needed if adding magic-link sign-in.
- No database client/ORM (no `pg`, `prisma`, `drizzle-orm`, `mongodb`, etc.).
- No `@clerk/nextjs` installed yet, but `docs/clerk.md` (see below) documents exactly how to add it.

---

## 7. Directory structure

```
src/
├── auth.ts                                  # NextAuth config (providers, session, callbacks)
├── proxy.ts                                  # route-protection middleware (matches /dashboard/:path*)
├── lib/
│   └── users.ts                              # in-memory user store + auth helper functions
└── app/
    ├── layout.tsx                            # root layout; renders header w/ session-aware nav
    ├── page.tsx                              # default create-next-app landing page (unmodified)
    ├── globals.css                           # Tailwind v4 import + CSS vars
    ├── favicon.ico
    ├── sign-out-button.tsx                   # client component, calls next-auth/react signOut()
    ├── signin/page.tsx                       # client-rendered sign-in form (Google + credentials)
    ├── signup/page.tsx                       # client-rendered sign-up form (calls /api/signup then signIn)
    ├── dashboard/page.tsx                    # protected page; shows current user + all users
    └── api/
        ├── auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts       # NextAuth handlers (GET/POST)
        └── signup/route.ts                   # custom credentials sign-up endpoint
```
No `src/components/` directory, no `src/app/account/` yet. App Router only (no `pages/` directory anywhere).

---

## 8. Env vars

`.env.example`:
```
AUTH_SECRET=placeholder_generate_with_openssl_rand_base64_32
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=placeholder
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=placeholder
```
- No `.env` file currently present (git-ignored via `.env*` in `.gitignore`).
- `AUTH_SECRET` read implicitly by NextAuth (Auth.js convention, not referenced explicitly in code).
- `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` / `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` read directly in `src/auth.ts`.
- No email/SMTP env vars exist yet (would be needed for magic links, e.g. `EMAIL_SERVER`, `EMAIL_FROM`, or a provider API key like Resend).

There's also `docs/clerk.md` and `llms.txt` at the repo root, which read like they were deliberately placed to guide a migration to Clerk:

`llms.txt`:
```
# Clerk
> Authentication and user management for web apps: sign up, sign in, social login, sessions, protected routes.
## Docs
- [Next.js quickstart](docs/clerk.md): install, environment variables, provider, middleware, protected routes
```

`docs/clerk.md` (76 lines) documents, step by step:
1. `npm install @clerk/nextjs`
2. Env vars: `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`, `CLERK_SECRET_KEY`
3. Wrap app in `<ClerkProvider>` in `layout.tsx`
4. `src/middleware.ts` using `clerkMiddleware` + `createRouteMatcher(["/dashboard(.*)"])`
5. Sign-in/up pages via prebuilt `<SignIn />` component
6. Server-side `auth()` / `currentUser()` from `@clerk/nextjs/server`

This strongly suggests the task this repo is set up for is: **migrate off NextAuth/in-memory users onto Clerk** (or similarly add magic-link + account page, matching Clerk's model where email+password and social are dashboard-configured, not code-configured).

---

## 9. Styling approach

- **Tailwind CSS v4** (`@tailwindcss/postcss` + `tailwindcss: ^4`), configured via `postcss.config.mjs`:
  ```js
  export default { plugins: { "@tailwindcss/postcss": {} } };
  ```
- `globals.css` uses the new Tailwind v4 `@import "tailwindcss";` + `@theme inline` syntax, defining `--color-background`/`--color-foreground` CSS vars driven by `prefers-color-scheme` (dark mode support built in), plus Geist Sans/Mono fonts loaded via `next/font/google` in `layout.tsx`.
- No component library (no shadcn/ui, no MUI, no Chakra) — everything is hand-rolled Tailwind utility classes.
- Consistent card/form pattern used on both `signin/page.tsx` and `signup/page.tsx`, useful as a template for new pages (e.g. `/account`, magic-link sign-in):
  - Full-height centered flex container: `flex flex-1 items-center justify-center bg-zinc-50 px-4 py-16 dark:bg-black`
  - Card: `w-full max-w-sm space-y-6 rounded-xl border border-black/[.08] bg-white p-8 dark:border-white/[.145] dark:bg-zinc-950`
  - Heading: `text-xl font-semibold text-black dark:text-zinc-50`, subtext `text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400`
  - OAuth button: `flex h-11 w-full items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-black/[.08] px-5 text-sm font-medium transition-colors hover:bg-black/[.04] dark:border-white/[.145] dark:hover:bg-[#1a1a1a]`
  - "or" divider: flex row with `h-px flex-1 bg-black/[.08] dark:bg-white/[.145]` lines around uppercase text
  - Text inputs: `w-full rounded-md border border-black/[.08] bg-transparent px-3 py-2 text-sm outline-none focus:border-black/40 dark:border-white/[.145] dark:focus:border-white/40`
  - Primary submit button (pill, inverted colors): `flex h-11 w-full items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-foreground px-5 text-sm font-medium text-background transition-colors hover:bg-[#383838] disabled:opacity-60 dark:hover:bg-[#ccc]`
  - Error text: `text-sm text-red-600 dark:text-red-400`
- `layout.tsx` header nav pattern (session-aware): `flex items-center justify-between border-b border-black/[.08] px-6 py-4 text-sm dark:border-white/[.145]`, shows Dashboard link + email + Sign out when authenticated, Sign in/Sign up links otherwise. Any new `/account` link should slot in here similarly.

---

## 10. Versions / project config

- **Node**: v22.22.2 (from local environment)
- **Next.js**: `16.3.4` — App Router only (no `pages/` dir; `src/app/` used throughout). Note the use of `LayoutProps<"/">` typed prop in `layout.tsx`, a newer Next typegen convention.
- **React**: 19.2.8 / react-dom 19.2.8
- **TypeScript**: `^5`, strict mode on. Key `tsconfig.json` settings:
